WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.621
The pieces come together under one rule:

2
00:00:02.621 --> 00:00:06.438
match each flow's consistency
needs to its transport class.

3
00:00:06.438 --> 00:00:10.764
Only authoritative writes and
in-region quorum ride the lean path,

4
00:00:10.764 --> 00:00:13.675
and neither crosses a
region synchronously.

5
00:00:13.675 --> 00:00:16.412
At the branch, four
patterns cover practice.

6
00:00:16.412 --> 00:00:20.313
The hairpin is assessed, but
every flow pays the detour.

7
00:00:20.313 --> 00:00:24.374
Bare local breakout isn't an
option in the TIC use case at all.

8
00:00:24.374 --> 00:00:26.071
Governed local breakout,

9
00:00:26.071 --> 00:00:30.350
an SD-WAN edge plus a nearby SASE
point, is the reference pattern.

10
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:34.175
And agent-delivered SASE
suits small and roaming sites.

11
00:00:34.175 --> 00:00:38.216
Then five decisions carry most of
the risk: one writer per region,

12
00:00:38.216 --> 00:00:41.877
a written path policy, the
boundary change before cutover,

13
00:00:41.877 --> 00:00:47.062
the governor protected before it carries
traffic, and the path made into evidence.

14
00:00:47.062 --> 00:00:49.975
Each fails quietly, so
each comes with a check.

15
00:00:49.975 --> 00:00:51.620
Who makes those decisions?
